 "response": "Gitrel's budget is now **$2805K**, by my count. I traced it by hand across about 1,600 records and did not re-add the full sequence independently, so treat it as one careful count rather than a double-checked figure.\n\n**How I worked it out**\n- **Source:** Only Finance Office messages count. All budget figures from Sales, Legal, Engineering, PMO, Operations, Facilities, Marketing and Vendor calls are ignored.\n- **Starting point:** Finance set the budget to $2220K in #0001.\n- **Withdrawals:** For every withdrawal, I traced its full chain, because withdrawals can themselves be withdrawn. Where a chain was broken at some point, the withdrawal just below the break stands again. Examples:\n  - #0537 withdraws #0092. That revives #0071, which voids #0033, so #0005 stands and #0002 stays withdrawn.\n  - #1348 withdraws #0194. That revives #0170, which voids #0009, so the +$288K in #0008 counts.\n  - #1541 withdraws #1356. That revives #1257, which voids #0951, so the +$22K in #0503 counts.\n  - #0770 withdraws the +$112K in #0026.\n- **Calculation:** Starting from $2220K, I applied every Finance Office increase and decrease that was still in effect, once each and in record order. The last effective change is \u2212$50K in #1600, which brings the running total to $2805K.\n\nANSWER: $2805K",
